From: BananaDS <bananads@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 95/95] LAN: one session after another in the same run, and discovery
 beside a host

A frontend that ends a LAN session and starts another in the same run (BananaDS's in-game LAN page: host, then
disconnect and join someone else) got the old session's players, connected and MP-active bits, miss counts and
last host back in the new one. EndSession now clears them.

The discovery socket gets SO_REUSEADDR before its bind, so a host and a player looking for hosts on the same
machine (or a frontend restarting discovery right after ending a session) both hear the hosts' broadcasts.

Wifi::IsPoweredOn() tells the frontend whether the game's wifi is already on when a session starts, so it can
call MP_Begin for it (melonDS called it before there was a session to tell).
---
 src/Wifi.h      |  2 ++
 src/net/LAN.cpp | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Wifi.h b/src/Wifi.h
index 870c5e2..36595f4 100644
--- a/src/Wifi.h
+++ b/src/Wifi.h
@@ -174,6 +174,8 @@ public:
     const u8* GetBSSID() const;
     // BananaDS: the game's Wi-Fi is in a local multiplayer mode (host beaconing or client synced)
     bool InMPMode() const { return IsMP; }
+    // BananaDS: the game's Wi-Fi is powered on (Platform::MP_Begin was called and MP_End not since)
+    bool IsPoweredOn() const { return PowerOn; }
 
 private:
     melonDS::NDS& NDS;
diff --git a/src/net/LAN.cpp b/src/net/LAN.cpp
index 249a6f6..3364660 100644
--- a/src/net/LAN.cpp
+++ b/src/net/LAN.cpp
@@ -248,6 +248,11 @@ bool LAN::StartDiscovery()
         return false;
     }
 
+    // BananaDS: more than one listener on the discovery port (a host and a player looking for hosts on the same
+    // machine, as in the tests): each gets the broadcasts
+    int opt_reuse = 1;
+    setsockopt(DiscoverySocket, SOL_SOCKET, SO_REUSEADDR, (const char*)&opt_reuse, sizeof(int));
+
     sockaddr_in_t saddr;
     memset(&saddr, 0, sizeof(saddr));
     saddr.sin_family = AF_INET;
@@ -478,6 +483,19 @@ void LAN::EndSession()
     enet_host_destroy(Host);
     Host = nullptr;
     IsHost = false;
+
+    // BananaDS: nothing of this session carries over into the next one (the frontend can end a session and start
+    // another in the same run): its players, who was connected, who was in a DS group with us
+    Platform::Mutex_Lock(PlayersMutex);
+    memset(Players, 0, sizeof(Players));
+    NumPlayers = 0;
+    MaxPlayers = 0;
+    Platform::Mutex_Unlock(PlayersMutex);
+    ConnectedBitmask = 0;
+    MPActiveBitmask = 0;
+    memset(MPMissCount, 0, sizeof(MPMissCount));
+    LastHostID = -1;
+    LastHostPeer = nullptr;
 }
 
 
